# Texture Material Prep commands and isolated UE proof

Companion to the [foundation contract](TEXTURE_MATERIAL_PREP.md), Issue #382.
This page separates offline diagnostics, the opt-in editor adapter and pending production gates.
For the subsequently approved local activation, real-source proof and remote
backup, read the [remote continuation report](TEXTURE_MATERIAL_PREP_REMOTE_HANDOFF.md).

## Implemented commands

Run from the repository root, normally the canonical project described in
[the workspace guide](LOCAL_WORKSPACE.md), using its existing Python environment.
The tool uses NumPy and Pillow already pinned by the hosted Python test lane;
it adds no dependency, service or MCP server.

```powershell
# Filesystem capability facts only; does not connect to or launch Unreal.
python scripts/assets/texture_material_prep.py capabilities `
  --project YetAnotherCyclingSim.uproject `
  --engine-root D:/yacs/engine/UE_5.8

# Use the exact source file you have resolved and provenance-reviewed.
# A supplied 2 x 2 m size is recorded as proposed, never automatically accepted.
python scripts/assets/texture_material_prep.py analyze `
  --source path/to/YACS_SC_Limestone_01_BaseColor.png `
  --input-color-space srgb --world-size-m 2 2

# Compare two images of matching resolution and declared sRGB transfer.
python scripts/assets/texture_material_prep.py analyze `
  --source path/to/candidate.png --baseline path/to/source.png `
  --input-color-space srgb

# Prepare a deterministic draft recipe. This does not render anything.
python scripts/assets/texture_material_prep.py plan `
  --source path/to/YACS_SC_Limestone_01_BaseColor.png `
  --input-color-space srgb --resolution 512
```

The source paths above are placeholders, not bundled or discovered assets.
Resolve engine location from the actual workspace configuration; the example
path is the inspected reference host. `capabilities` emits JSON on stdout.
`analyze` and `plan` print the new evidence directory under
`Saved/RuntimeProof/TextureMaterialPrep/<generated_uuid>/`.
Existing files are never overwritten. Evidence is ignored by Git; source bytes
are read and preserved. Exit 0 means a report/plan was produced, including a
blocked plan or review-required result. Exit 2 means invalid input or an IO error.

An optional `--parameters path/to/parameters.json` accepts exactly the documented
parameter keys, for example:

```json
{
  "SeamBlendWidth": 0.05,
  "DeLightStrength": 0.25,
  "ColorGain": [1.0, 1.0, 1.0],
  "HeightStrength": 0.5,
  "NormalStrength": 1.0,
  "RoughnessMin": 0.55,
  "RoughnessMax": 0.9,
  "MacroVariation": 0.0,
  "Seed": 0,
  "GenerateAO": false
}
```

Unknown keys, non-finite/bool numbers, out-of-range parameters, reversed roughness
limits, non-integer seeds and enabled AO are rejected. Draft recipe IDs hash the
source identity and canonical plan. They are **not execution identities**:
`graph_hash`, `engine_build` and `execution_identity` are null and the plan
returns `blocked / UE_CONNECTION_REQUIRED`. The editor adapter creates its own run receipt with graph package hash, source
data GUID, exact engine build and recipe. Offline draft IDs are never accepted
as executable job IDs. A full transitive dependency identity remains deferred.

### Supported subset

| Implemented now | Still deferred |
|---|---|
| Opaque RGB/RGBA 8-bit PNG BaseColor analysis, 8..4096 px, <=64 MiB | HDR, profiled/16-bit inputs and calibrated displacement |
| Opt-in UE 5.8.2 fixed native graph, async named renders, exact-pixel serialization and five-map readback | Main project activation and reusable promoted graph template |
| Seam/luminance metrics, normal unit length and angular seam metrics, 2x2/4x4 previews | Compressed GPU/mip readback, DirectX ramp and visual acceptance |
| Exact engine build, graph package hash, source GUID/PNG SHA-256, proposed world scale | Full dependency manifest, accepted limestone coverage/provenance |
| Native Toolset Registry definition, scoped db-lyon guard and isolated profile | End-to-end remote MCP transport admission and texture broker command |

The decoder rejects ICC/chromaticity profiles, conflicting PNG gamma, animation,
non-opaque alpha, grayscale and 16-bit PNG rather than silently reinterpret or
downconvert them. It is intentionally not a general image importer. The original
file's bytes are hashed from the same bounded read that is decoded.

Numerical screening uses the provisional BaseColor policy in the contract.
`within_provisional_limits` is only a screen. `admission` stays `review_required`,
`ue_validation` stays `not_run`, and `visual_acceptance` stays `pending`.
Even a perfect constant image cannot become an admitted limestone material.

Reports use linear values. Diagnostic PNGs retain sRGB display pixels and never
serve as production outputs. Contact sheets have a maximum 256-pixel tile edge;
native seam/corner crops are separate. The receipt hashes every generated report
and preview except itself. It is not an exact-SHA UE proof receipt. On an IO
failure, partial evidence may remain in its new run directory; it is not accepted.

```powershell
python scripts/assets/test_texture_material_prep.py
python scripts/ci/check_docs_index.py
python scripts/ci/test_final_architecture_contract.py
```

The test file follows existing `test_*.py` discovery, so the hosted Python lane
runs it without workflow changes. Synthetic cases check sRGB transfer, both axes,
equal-edge gradient defects, zero-denominator JSON, luminance changes, invalid
inputs/parameters, PNG precision, metadata, no-overwrite and CLI evidence hashes.

## Implemented opt-in editor adapter

The plugin descriptor is disabled by default. Do not add it to the canonical
project or copy over its live MCP configuration for this test. Reserve at least
50 GiB free disk under the workspace policy. Use a new proof directory; UAT
clears an existing packaging destination. Compile only this plugin, not YACS.
Resolve the engine/work roots from `workspace.json`; these are the reference
host's paths. Run from the isolated repository checkout:

```powershell
$engineRoot = 'D:/yacs/engine/UE_5.8'
$repoRoot = (Get-Location).Path
$proofRoot = Join-Path 'D:/yacs/work' ('texture-prep-proof-' + [Guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N'))
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $proofRoot) { throw 'Proof destination must be new' }
& "$engineRoot/Engine/Build/BatchFiles/RunUAT.bat" BuildPlugin `
  "-Plugin=$repoRoot/Plugins/YacsTexturePrep/YacsTexturePrep.uplugin" `
  "-Package=$proofRoot" -TargetPlatforms=Win64 -StrictIncludes -NoDeleteHostProject
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'Plugin build failed' }
$proofProject = "$proofRoot/HostProject/HostProject.uproject"
New-Item "$proofRoot/HostProject/.yacs-texture-prep-proof" -ItemType File | Out-Null
Start-Process "$engineRoot/Engine/Binaries/Win64/UnrealEditor.exe" -WindowStyle Hidden `
  -ArgumentList @($proofProject, '-unattended', '-nosplash', '-nosound', '-NoLiveCoding',
    '-RenderOffscreen', '-ZenDataPath=D:/yacs/cache/Zen', "-ExecutePythonScript=$repoRoot/scripts/assets/texture_material_prep_ue_smoke.py")
```

The smoke generates a deliberately discontinuous 128x128 PNG, imports it into a
new fixture folder, registers only `YacsTexturePrep.YacsTextureTools`, verifies
its schema and dispatch, then prepares, renders, exports and reads back five
maps. It owns and quits only the disposable editor. Engine shutdown/exit 0 is
**not success**: require a `texture-smoke-<uuid>/result.json` under that project's
Saved directory with `exported_review_required`, no failure receipt, and a
registry probe. The result contains the bundle evidence directory.

Run diagnostics on that directory with the repository Python environment:

```powershell
python scripts/assets/texture_material_prep_bundle.py path/to/bundle
# After the fresh-editor reopen script:
python scripts/assets/texture_material_prep_bundle.py path/to/bundle --reopen path/to/reopen-evidence
python -m unittest discover -s scripts/assets -p 'test_texture_material_prep*.py'
node --test tools/ue-mcp/guards/YacsTextureGuard.test.js
```

The validator exits 1 on detected degenerate BaseColor, out-of-range roughness or
non-unit normal vectors. Other seam/de-light screens remain review gates. Linear
map channels are not sRGB-decoded. All previews are diagnostic; no image is
processed into a production output by Python.

After diagnostics, launch the **same proof project in a fresh editor process**
with `texture_material_prep_ue_reopen.py` in place of the smoke script. It verifies
the graph package hash and reopened texture dimensions/color/compression, then
exports source-mip PNGs into a new `reopen-<uuid>` directory. The `--reopen` validator compares all five
decoded PNG arrays to the original bundle; settings success alone does not prove
pixel durability. It does not rerun the graph or save any asset.

### Tool calls and guarded MCP routing

Explicit registration in the proof editor:

```python
unreal.ToolsetRegistry.register_toolset_class(unreal.YacsTextureTools)
```

`InspectCapabilities`, `PrepareTexture`, `RenderPreview`, `ExportPbrSet`,
`ValidateTexture`, `GetJobStatus` are the six native operations. Their JSON schema
is generated from the compiled definitions; inputs use camelCase (`jobId`,
`sourceAssetPath`, `recipe`). Registry results wrap the JSON report in
`returnValue`. Direct Python methods use snake_case names. `PrepareTexture`
accepts a saved source object path and `YacsTextureRecipe`; it creates a fixed
new graph, not arbitrary caller-authored nodes. WorldSizeMeters is required as a
positive hypothesis, never assumed to be accepted limestone coverage.

For a db-lyon integration test, copy `tools/ue-mcp/texture-proof-profile.yml` as
`ue-mcp.yml` **only in the disposable project**, with the pinned package and
`tools/ue-mcp/guards/YacsTextureGuard.js` available at the declared relative path.
Bind that client to the proof editor, not the open authoring project. Keep
`nativeTools.enabled: false`: the narrow `epic.call_tool` gateway still works;
the guard rejects other toolsets, Python, console commands and arbitrary writes.
Do not enable `All Toolsets` or start an additional native MCP server.

Example gateway payload:

```json
{
  "action": "call_tool",
  "toolset": "YacsTexturePrep.YacsTextureTools",
  "tool": "YacsTexturePrep.YacsTextureTools.InspectCapabilities",
  "input": {}
}
```

The engine registry's direct `ExecuteTool` API expects the **bare** operation
name. db-lyon 1.3.9 strips the qualifier before dispatch. Never bypass the guard
with an alternate `inputJson` channel. Poll job status between phases: a timeout
means the task is draining, not cancelled. Do not retry a write on the same job.

### Required negative UE integration cases

| Trigger | Required outcome |
|---|---|
| Plugin disabled, reflected name missing, settings enum unsupported | Structured unsupported result before mutation; no generic Python fallback |
| Wrong/missing parameter that native API would only warn about | Preflight/readback rejection; never report a successful stage |
| Unknown role, duplicate output, hidden output outside run root | Abort before export |
| Existing asset, package, name collision or path traversal | Abort; byte-identical pre-existing content |
| Source/template changes between preview and export | New plan required |
| Concurrent job, timeout, exception, late completion | Bounded status, lock held until native completion; no late acceptance |
| Void export return but missing/wrong asset, precision loss or sRGB mismatch | `EXPORT_INCOMPLETE` / failed validation; no success receipt |
| Good metrics but unknown physical coverage or strong baked light | Review/scale gate remains open |
| Successful export and save but fresh reopen differs | Reject durability proof |

No `/yacs-editor texture-*` command exists. Do not paste tool calls into a generic
remote executor or bypass the current `smoke-cube` allowlist.

## Authorized local seven-role library

On 2026-10-05 the owner requested every missing 2B surface material through the
existing UE generator. This authorizes new local source imports, native Texture
Graph output packages and separate preview materials in the already open editor;
it does not assign them to the Landscape or admit a production surface set.
The earlier disposable-project instructions above remain the isolated proof path.

[The library producer](../../scripts/assets/generate_sa_calobra_texture_library_ue.py)
reads [the pinned manifest](../../worldgen/materials/sa_calobra_texture_library_20261005.json).
With the recorded texture checkpoint open, execute the producer from Unreal's
Tools > Execute Python Script menu. It requires the exact project/map and source
hashes, serializes seven jobs, and writes unique source, graph, texture and material
packages. It refuses collisions and stops on native task failure or timeout.
Do not launch another batch while a previous native task is draining.

Roles: ExposedRock, Scree, DryMineral, DryGrass, ForestLitter, RockCut and
FillGravel. RockCut deliberately reuses the exposed-rock source with stronger
normal detail; it is not another scan. Six immutable Poly Haven Diffuse sources
are reused under the explicit local-generation approval in the provenance ledger.
Provider scales are retained. No de-light, colour gain or seam blending is applied
to the already tiled source baseline. Each graph generates 1024-square BaseColor,
Normal, Roughness, Height and MacroMask. Only BaseColor, Normal and Roughness are
connected to the preview material; UV0 spans one tile. Height remains an artistic
image-derived map, with no displacement or world geometry modification.

Results appear under `/Game/Generated/YACS/TextureMaterialPrep/Libraries/<uuid>`
(materials and source imports), native `Runs/<job-id>` (maps and graph), and
`Saved/RuntimeProof/TextureLibraries/<uuid>` (manifest and receipts).
A `generated_review_required` receipt requires seven completed jobs plus an
unchanged saved-map hash and actor identity/transform inventory. This is not
visual, compressed GPU, fresh-editor persistence or performance acceptance.
Run the existing bundle validator on every completed native evidence directory;
report seam flags separately from structural diagnostics. Never rerun just
because a partial library exists: inspect its result first and retain its bytes.

The 2026-10-05 completed run is recorded in
[the library result](../../worldgen/materials/sa_calobra_texture_library_result_20261005.json):
seven saved materials and 35 maps, with seven successful structural diagnostics
and no diagnostic flags. Visual acceptance, compressed GPU sampling and
fresh-editor reopening remain pending. The map hash and actor inventory matched.

The producer guards Slate callback reentry: native imports and exports can pump
editor ticks before returning. Without that guard, the same source was imported
again into its newly created package and `bReplaceExisting=false` correctly
rejected the duplicate. Three callback regression tests cover nested import ticks,
failure cleanup and repeated completion; previous failed-run packages are retained.

### Applying the generated library to Landscape

The owner subsequently authorized Landscape application and a separate review
map. [The generated-surface consumer](../../scripts/ue/apply_sa_calobra_generated_surfaces.py)
must run in the open texture checkpoint. It verifies the saved checkpoint hash
and existing v3 mask inputs, then uses native WorldAlignedTexture and
WorldAlignedNormal functions with provider tile dimensions. Generated Roughness
textures require a Masks sampler, matching their native compression setting.

DryMineral supplies residual presentation ground; the existing R/G/B mask
channels select a limited DryGrass contribution, ForestLitter and ExposedRock.
The dry-fibre default is 0.35 of the existing open-ground amplitude, an artistic
contribution rather than a cover measurement. Scree, RockCut and FillGravel stay
unmapped until dedicated geographic masks are available. This consumer does not
invent classifications or modify masks, terrain, road geometry or displacement.
It saves only its new material/weight packages and a uniquely named review map,
retaining the original checkpoint bytes. Receipts under
`Saved/RuntimeProof/TextureLandscape/<uuid>` distinguish geometry checks, native
render-instance checks, visual acceptance and pending performance/reopen proof.

The [2026-10-05 Landscape result](../../worldgen/materials/sa_calobra_generated_landscape_result_20261005.json)
records the saved review map, same-editor reload and fresh-process reload with
the assigned material and 1024 unchanged components. The
[reload verifier](../../scripts/ue/verify_sa_calobra_generated_surface_map.py)
compares actor transforms, topology, edit-layer names, nine collision traces and
map hashes. The current binary lacks the native render-instance audit, so that
gate remains unavailable rather than reported as PASS. Visual/performance
acceptance remains pending.

For interactive authoring, execute scripts from the editor menu/console.
`-ExecutePythonScript` with keep-alive retains the startup notification after a
completed batch; clearing keep-alive or clicking its Cancel exits the editor.
The native executor's waiting tick does not rerun the completed generator.
After saving and verifying the review map, a normal restart removed that
notification. The batch session crashed in TextureGraph during shutdown after
the editor's shutdown log; its local crash report was retained and not sent.
The new process successfully read the saved map and material. This does not
establish the shutdown fault's root cause or a loading-performance improvement.

### Street View palette presentation variant

The owner approved a cooler limestone/mineral palette using their Street View
screenshots as an artistic reference. Run
`scripts/ue/apply_sa_calobra_surface_presentation.py` in the saved first review
map. Its tracked JSON recipe fixes that map's hash and creates another unique
material/map; it never overwrites the source review or texture checkpoint.
The optional consumer recipe adds native Desaturation and RGB gain nodes to
BaseColor. Normal/Roughness and provider detail scale retain their generated
inputs. DryGrass amplitude is `R * 0.35 * saturate((macro.R - 0.35) / 0.3)`;
the existing generated MacroMask is world-aligned at a decorative 12 m span.
This only reduces grass within the admitted R mask and preserves the mineral
residual, not a new geographic or measured seasonal classification.

The saved variant `L_SaCalobraGeneratedSurfaces_9992abd22044` passed native
compilation and same-editor reload, with 375 actor transforms, 1024 components,
edit layers and nine collision traces unchanged. Base Color and Lit were
inspected at the same viewport camera. The direct light was already white with
temperature disabled; no light settings were edited. The distant terrain still
appears broad and smooth, so this palette pass is not full scene realism or
owner visual acceptance. Dedicated Scree/RockCut/FillGravel masks, 3D vegetation,
fresh-process verification of this variant and performance acceptance remain
outside this result. A D3D12 GPU timeout warning occurred during compilation;
the editor recovered, saved and reloaded the variant. Its cause is unproven.

### Inspecting material mask channels

`scripts/ue/inspect_sa_calobra_mask_channels.py` creates native unlit RGB and
single-channel R/G/B/A materials, verifies the existing v3 input hashes and
saves/reloads a unique diagnostic map. The source presentation map is preserved.
In RGB, red means low-vegetation presentation amplitude, green means medium/high
vegetation forest-floor fallback, and blue means dated polygon rock share.
Black is zero RGB, not a bare-soil/rock classification. Individual channels are
grayscale; A is sample availability, not confidence or a surface class.
In the authoring session, `builtins.yacs_show_mask_channel('B')` switches only
this diagnostic map. Switching is a temporary map edit; restore RGB before
saving or loading another map.

The 2026-10-05 raw raster statistics show previous consumer average weights of
0.08864 DryGrass, 0.07650 ForestLitter, 0.08847 ExposedRock and 0.74639 DryMineral.
These are horizontal-grid blend amplitudes, not measured cover or 3D area.
The bounded grass macro in the later palette variant can only increase that
mineral residual. Zero RGB occupies 28.444% of cells; 16.684% have no observed
LiDAR samples. Every excluded cell retains zero RGB. Source exclusion reasons
overlap and include route/earthworks, context, other LiDAR classes and missing
samples. The pixel alignment/holdback contract passing does not establish that
these broad fallback domains reproduce visible rock/soil/vegetation boundaries.

### Owner-authorized inferred appearance in mask gaps

On 2026-10-05 the owner explicitly authorized filling black diagnostic areas
from artistic inference rather than leaving every missing classification as
uniform mineral ground. `scripts/ue/apply_sa_calobra_inferred_gap_fill.py`
preserves the inspected diagnostic map, opens the hash-pinned palette review,
and saves another unique review material/map through the existing consumer.
Raw RGB sum zero selects the fallback: `saturate(1 - 1000 * sumRGB)` is exactly
zero for every nonzero 8-bit input sum. Steeper terrain receives more limestone
using `saturate(((1 - abs(VertexNormalWS.Z)) - 0.06) / 0.34)`; gentle gaps receive
up to 0.22 dry-grass contribution multiplied by the existing decorative macro.
Mineral ground remains the complement, so total surface weights remain one.

This is explicitly inferred appearance, including the visual fallback over
source holdbacks. Source PNG/TIFF weights, geographic classifications, unknown
flags and PCG/placement exclusions remain unchanged. It does not admit plants,
rocks, soil subtype or structures as measured facts and adds no geometry, WPO
or displacement. Vertex normals come from the rendered Landscape geometry;
the slope appearance can depend on its rendered LOD. Normal authoring receipts
and geometry/persistence checks still apply; visual/performance acceptance is
separate from the owner's authorization to infer this fallback.

### Separated shading domains and interrupted native proof (2026-10-05)

Public Embark references describe layered biome assets, scan cleanup/de-lighting,
detail maps and LiDAR/Houdini export to Unreal. They do not publish YACS exclusion
rules or a hydrological reconstruction recipe:
- https://www.sidefx.com/learn/talks/embark-landscape-creation/
- https://medium.com/embarkstudios/working-with-photogrammetry-in-practice-1f9dada77606
- https://medium.com/embarkstudios/from-photos-to-in-game-assets-23c2f5e5d08

`prepare_sa_calobra_surface_domains.py` derives presentation classes from retained
LiDAR counts before placement exclusions. The PCG masks remain immutable and
binding. On the frozen 4033 grid it restores nonzero RGB in 1,883,226 previously
zero cells; 2,713,728 unknown-sample cells remain explicitly unknown in a separate
availability PNG. Alpha is now a dry-channel artistic overlay, not availability.
The bounded one-metre half-width around mapped water lines is a YACS decision,
not a surveyed channel width or Embark setting. Point springs and reservoirs do
not become channels. Road/building pixels suppress this overlay. The retained
context contains both BTN and provisional regional hydrography; source dates and
positional/completeness limits remain inherited.

The native five-role plus macro-variation attempt `7130b3a81d29415d8fc8d239d66b4a21`
crashed before a completion receipt or saved review map. D3D12 reported
E_OUTOFMEMORY, Windows reported no available virtual memory and an insufficient
page file. Peak reported virtual usage was 66.47 GiB. This proves exhaustion,
not the precise allocation owner or mask corruption. Crash data is retained
locally; it was not transmitted. The prior saved map `24761d13ffbd` remains at
SHA-256 `98f9440961019ebc237e4a3c702bd17d771efaaf8bb7c8c40f08e89066141582`.

After the owner requested gentler iteration, `apply_sa_calobra_surface_domains.py`
stages only four roles with `prepare_only=True`, no new dry-channel layer and no
extra macro samples. The material is compiled/saved without Landscape assignment
or review-map save. This revised native path is NOT YET EXECUTED or accepted.
A lightweight material preview and resource check must precede whole-Landscape
assignment; add the channel overlay and macro variation individually afterwards.
No page-file/system setting change or editor restart was performed automatically.
PCGEx is already a pinned authoring dependency and remains the later placement
consumer. Embark texture-synthesis is research only: its repository is archived
and explicitly says the studio is not actively using/developing it. No new
third-party code or Rust dependency was introduced.

The surface-domain entry point now advances exactly one wave per explicit script
invocation: weight import, one role graph at a time, output wiring, compile call,
and save. State remains in the current UE process, so rerunning resumes without
reimporting or duplicating assets. There is no automatic timer or retry. Windows
memory admission requires at least 8 GiB available physical and 12 GiB available
commit before each wave; these are conservative YACS operational thresholds,
not a guarantee. A compile/import/save call can still block or exhaust memory
inside a wave. COMPILE_CALL_RETURNED does not prove all background shaders have
finished; let their work settle before explicitly continuing.

The already-open clean recorded map is used, with no map switch or map save.
Changed/dirty maps reject continuation. The entry point always stages four roles
without the dry-channel overlay/new macro samples and never assigns to Landscape.
An editor restart loses live iterator state; it does not automatically replay
unfinished work. Eleven boundary/scheduler tests and Ruff passed; execution of
this revised native wave path remains pending. Suggested commit:
`Separate surface domains and stage native material preparation in manual waves`.

`preview_sa_calobra_surface_component.py` provides the next bounded native proof:
one component nearest the current camera receives OverrideMaterial through
set_editor_property; running the same script again restores that override and
camera. It never calls LandscapeComponent.SetMaterial, which UE 5.8.2 source
shows writes the entire proxy's LandscapeMaterial. Native PostEditChangeProperty
for OverrideMaterial updates only this component's material instances. No map
save or geometry operation is performed. Original map hash, geometry, global
material and all other component overrides are checked; memory admission uses
the same operational thresholds. Do not Save/Save All during this session preview.
Ruff and Python syntax checks passed; actual execution/render acceptance is
pending. Suggested commit: `Add reversible single-component surface preview`.
